      "dom_id": "question-100672",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Use a calculator to evaluate ${log}_{7}⁡(12)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's calculate ${log}_{7}⁡(12)$ by changing the base $7$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).\n\nWe use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=7,$ $X=12,$ $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{7}⁡(12) & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(12)}{{log}_{10}⁡(7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(12)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{1.079\\,18}{0.845\\,10} \\\\  & ≈1.28\\end{aligned}\n$$",
