      "problem": "Calculate ${log}_{36}⁡(216)$ without using a calculator.",
      "worked_solution": "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=36,$ and $X=216.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ are powers of $6,$ we set $b=6.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{36}⁡(216) & =\\frac{{log}_{6}⁡(216)}{{log}_{6}⁡(36)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{6}⁡({6}^{3})}{{log}_{6}⁡({6}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
